 Ansible + CI/CD

🔹 PHASE 5: DevOps Integration
Today I learned how Ansible integrates with CI/CD pipelines to automate deployments and infrastructure changes seamlessly 🚀
Instead of manual deployments, Ansible can be triggered automatically through CI/CD tools.
 This ensures faster, consistent, and error-free releases ⚡

🔹 🔄 Ansible with GitHub Actions
Ansible can be integrated with CI/CD workflows using GitHub Actions.
Workflow:
 • Push code to repository
 • Trigger pipeline automatically
 • Run Ansible Playbooks for deployment
This enables fully automated deployment pipelines with zero manual intervention 📦

🔹 🛠️ Jenkins Integration
Ansible works very well with Jenkins for continuous deployment.
Common pipeline flow:
 • Build application
 • Run tests
 • Execute Ansible Playbook
 • Deploy to servers
Jenkins + Ansible = Powerful DevOps automation 🔥

🔹 🚀 Automated Deployments
Using Ansible in CI/CD helps in:
 • Automated server configuration
 • Application deployments
 • Rolling updates
 • Infrastructure provisioning
This reduces human errors and ensures consistent deployments across environments 🌍
Automated deployments are a core practice in modern DevOps pipelines.

